  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "            The notes on Unit 2 explain several useful expressions. \nIn Spanish, the question word '¿Cómo?' is often used alone to mean 'What did you say?' when someone does not hear or understand and wants a repetition. \nThe reflexive construction 'se dice' gives an impersonal meaning equivalent to 'it is said'. \nElevator instructions use the verbs 'sube' for 'goes up' and 'baja' for 'goes down'. \nThese simple expressions help learners navigate everyday conversations and contexts.\n"
    }
